<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <LangVersion>14</LangVersion>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <WarningsAsErrors>CS8509</WarningsAsErrors>
        <Title>DiffToJson.Lib</Title>
        <Authors>Alastair Lundy</Authors>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageId>DiffToJson.Lib</PackageId>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) Alastair Lundy 2026</Copyright>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/alastairlundy/difftojson</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageReleaseNotes># Changes since 0.7.0

## Added
- File access in the library now goes through an injectable file system, so tests can run without touching the real file system.
- After the models.dev catalog loads, reading supported reasoning values no longer waits on a network request.

## Changed
- `RunInputs` is replaced by `RawValue`, `RunRawInput`, and `RunTrainingInput`.
- Reasoning effort mapping is now documented and tested. OpenAI-style providers map `auto` and `on` to `medium`, and send `none` for `off`. Anthropic Effort models omit the property for `auto` and `on`, and send `reasoning_effort: off` for `off`.
- Extraction uses less memory during JSONL writing, PII redaction, prompt substitution, and git log parsing.
- Updated dependencies, including `CliInvoke` 3.2.0-beta.1, `Anthropic` 13.13.0, `Microsoft.Extensions.AI` packages 11.0.1, `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection` 11.0.0, `System.CommandLine` 3.0.0, and `TUnit` 1.87.12.

## Removed
- Removed the old hardcoded `ReasoningEffortMatrix`. Supported reasoning values now come from the models.dev catalog, with a small manual exception for MiniMax M-series models and `deepseek-chat`.

## Fixed
- Built-in prompt presets failed to load because placeholder names were parsed as empty. The placeholder pattern now captures names correctly.
- Provider ids are now lowercased in a culture-safe way, so they resolve correctly in cultures such as Turkish.

## Security
- The publish-nuget workflow now pins GitHub-owned actions by hash.
- `SECURITY.md` now documents dependency advisories.</PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
        <Version>0.8.0</Version>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DiffToJsonLib.Tests" />
